//! detect_execution_mode() : donnot work as expected
//! it is not working at all

// ==========================================
// ROADMAP & COMPILER ARCHITECTURE TODOs
// ==========================================
// 1. Compiler Warning & Dead Code Cleanup:
//    - Clean up temporary `#[allow(dead_code)]` attributes and unused underscore suppressions across compiler passes.
//    - Eliminate all compiler warning noise so builds are 100% clean.
//
// 2. detect_execution_mode Overhaul:
//    - Architectural refactoring of detect_execution_mode to cleanly distinguish between:
//      * FullyCompilable (pure compile-time only)
//      * DualMode (pure FastLang functions callable both at comptime and emitted for runtime)
//      * Mixed (contains static comptime branches/validations alongside runtime logic)
//      * RuntimeOnly (calls FFI/external C functions/system calls)
//
// 3. Web Compiler & Full DOM Stack:
//    - Advance src/std/html.fast to become a complete, robust HTML compiler supporting complex templates, large bodies, and full validation.
//    - Implement dedicated mini-parsers for CSS (src/std/css.fast) and JS (src/std/js.fast) following the html.fast slot & AST pattern.
//
// 4. FastReact Framework Automation:
//    - Build an interrupter / micro-parser for FastReact to automatically handle slot injection and reactive DOM updates without manual boilerplate.
//    - Core Philosophy: Fastest execution, least development effort, and minimum lines of code.
//
// 5. In-Place Blocks ({{ ... }}) & Template / Document String Injection:
//    - Semantics: In-place expressions and in-place blocks share the exact same underlying execution model.
//    - Control Flow: In-place blocks support full control flow (e.g. `for` loops inside `{{ for item in items { ... } }}`).
//    - Stringification & Injection via `display` Handle:
//      * When injecting components/structures (e.g., `header`) into a template (e.g., `page`):
//        Any injected object MUST be stringified via its `display` handle (`.display()`). (RULE: Strictly no `as_str`).
//      * The returned string is injected into the dynamic foreign template string.
//      * The foreign block parses this dynamic string into a `Document`, natively injecting it into the target document structure.
//    - HTML Parser Alternative Syntax:
//      * Support alternative block syntax in HTML templates to establish slots while keeping the slots switcher in the HTML parser fully intact.
//
// 6. Structural Equivalence (set Dog == Cat;):
//    - Equivalence Criteria: Subtyping/aliasing is determined STRICTLY by field types and memory layout order, NOT by field names.
//    - Memory Model: Matches C struct memory offsets (offset 0 type T1, offset 4 type T2, etc.).
//    - Interoperability: Allows passing `Dog` directly where `Cat` is expected with zero cast overhead, and enables shared `impl Cat, Dog` blocks.
//
// 7. Struct Capabilities Expansion & Native `share` Feature:
//    - Bring the `share` feature from `blueprint` into `struct` (`share <field> if (<cond>) [ { ... } ]`).
//    - Goal: Reduce reliance on `blueprint` by unifying all blueprint capabilities into `struct`.
//    - Native FastLang Semantics: Clarified that `share` is NOT C++ `shared_ptr`; it is FastLang's native copy/reference lifecycle rule as defined in `src/std/types.fast`.
//
// 8. Official Native C Backend:
//    - Top priority for this week: Finalize the official Native C backend to deliver a pure, zero-dependency, ultra-fast native backend.


